# shir_nodes/take_lines.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# Take first/last N lines or bytes (lowered from `head`/`tail`).
#
# Backends: Perl lines().take(), JS split().slice(), C fgets, Rust lines()
# Fallback: sh2.takeLines(text, count, from_end, bytes)

node TakeLines
tag "TakeLines"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field text: expr
field count: expr
field from_end: bool
field bytes: bool
spec: none (unstated: TakeLines is head/tail over a real line splitter —
# split on LF KEEPING empty fields (Perl split(/\n/,$t,-1), JS split('\n'), Java
# split("\n",-1)), take N fields from the front or back, rejoin with LF and add no
# terminator, so empty input is one empty line and "a\nb\n" is three. Stating that
# honestly needs an inverse-pair lemma (split ∘ join = id on newline-free chunks)
# plus a suffix law for the from-end arm; both were attempted in this session and
# did not close, so no law is approximated here.)
